# Package exports

A new export goes in BOTH `packages/<pkg>.lisp` AND the `packages/facade.lisp`
re-export. Miss the facade and CLI-package callers hit an undefined-function at
RUNTIME, while the unit layer stays green — only devnet-launching tests reach
that path, so this failure mode survives a clean unit run.

The architecture tests enforce package home-ownership. `facade.lisp` is the one
sanctioned mirror of the public surface; no other package may re-export a
symbol it does not own. When a symbol belongs somewhere else, move its home
rather than adding a re-export.

Before removing an internal symbol, grep `tests/` as well as `src/` for callers.
